
/*
QUERY NAME: Fall 2026 AI Conversation Faculty Adoption by Course

PURPOSE:
Identifies Blackboard Learn courses in the Fall 2026 term
that contain AI Conversation assessments.

The query counts the number of distinct AI Conversation
assessment records associated with each course and returns
the course ID, course name, term, and assigned instructors.

Results are organized by course ID, with courses having
the highest AI Conversation counts listed first.

This report can be used to evaluate faculty adoption of
Blackboard's AI Conversation feature across Fall 2026 courses.

DATA SOURCES:

1. LEARN.QTI_ASI_DATA (q)
   Referenced to identify AI Conversation assessment
   records and count distinct assessment identifiers.

   NOTE:
   This table and its fields are not included in the
   supplied valid_fields.pdf schema documentation.
   Its structure and the meaning of the filtering
   values require confirmation against the LEARN schema.

2. CDM_LMS.COURSE (c)
   Contains Blackboard course information, including
   course numbers, course names, term identifiers,
   and source identifiers.

3. CDM_LMS.TERM (t)
   Contains academic term information, including
   the term name.

4. CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE (pc)
   Connects users to courses and identifies their
   assigned course roles.

5. CDM_LMS.PERSON (p)
   Contains faculty names and Blackboard usernames
   stored in the STAGE JSON field.

TABLE RELATIONSHIPS:

1. COURSE.TERM_ID = TERM.ID
   Associates each course with its academic term.

2. PERSON_COURSE.COURSE_ID = COURSE.ID
   Associates instructor enrollments with courses.

3. PERSON_COURSE.PERSON_ID = PERSON.ID
   Connects instructor enrollments to person records.

4. AI_COUNTS.COURSE_SOURCE_ID =
   TRY_TO_NUMBER(COURSE.SOURCE_ID)

   Attempts to match AI Conversation assessment
   records to Blackboard courses using their
   source identifiers.

   IMPORTANT:
   This relationship cannot be validated using
   the supplied schema documentation because
   LEARN.QTI_ASI_DATA is not documented there.

------------------------------------------------------------
CTE 1: ai_counts
------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE:
Counts distinct AI Conversation assessment records
for each course source identifier.

SOURCE:
LEARN.QTI_ASI_DATA

COURSE IDENTIFICATION:

q.CRSMAIN_PK1 AS COURSE_SOURCE_ID

Uses the assessment record's CRSMAIN_PK1 value
to group assessments by course source identifier.

AI CONVERSATION COUNT:

COUNT(DISTINCT q.PK1) AS AI_COUNT

Counts distinct assessment record identifiers
within each course source identifier.

DISTINCT prevents duplicate occurrences of the
same PK1 from increasing the count.

FILTERING CONDITIONS:

1. q.BBMD_ASSESSMENT_SUBTYPE = 'AiConversation'

   Restricts results to records whose assessment
   subtype is identified as AiConversation.

2. q.BBMD_ASI_TYPE = 1

   Restricts results to assessment records with
   BBMD_ASI_TYPE equal to 1.

   The precise business meaning of this value
   requires confirmation from LEARN documentation.

3. q.ROW_DELETED_TIME IS NULL

   Excludes assessment records marked as deleted,
   assuming this field follows the documented
   CDM deletion timestamp convention.

GROUP BY:

q.CRSMAIN_PK1

Produces one aggregate record per course
source identifier.

EXAMPLE:

Course A:
- AI Conversation assessment 1
- AI Conversation assessment 2
- AI Conversation assessment 3

AI_COUNT = 3

IMPORTANT:
This is a count of distinct matching assessment
records, not a count of:
- Faculty members using AI Conversation.
- Student interactions with AI Conversation.
- AI Conversation attempts or submissions.
- Student participation.
- Time spent using AI Conversation.

------------------------------------------------------------
CTE 2: instructors
------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE:
Retrieves faculty assigned the Instructor role
in each course and combines their names and
Blackboard usernames into comma-separated fields.

SOURCE TABLES:
CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE
CDM_LMS.PERSON

INSTRUCTOR IDENTIFICATION:

pc.COURSE_ROLE = 'I'

Includes course enrollment records with the
Blackboard Instructor role.

pc.ROW_DELETED_TIME IS NULL

Excludes instructor enrollment records that
have been marked as deleted.

INSTRUCTOR NAME:

CONCAT(p.FIRST_NAME, ' ', p.LAST_NAME)

Combines each instructor's first and last name
into a single display name.

INSTRUCTOR_NAMES:

LISTAGG(DISTINCT ... , ', ')

Combines distinct instructor names into one
comma-separated field per course.

Example:
Jane Smith, Michael Jones

INSTRUCTOR_USERIDS:

p.STAGE:user_id::string

Extracts the Blackboard username from the
PERSON.STAGE JSON field.

LISTAGG combines distinct usernames into one
comma-separated field per course.

Example:
jsmith, mjones

WITHIN GROUP:
Sorts instructor names and usernames alphabetically
within their respective aggregated fields.

GROUP BY pc.COURSE_ID:
Produces one instructor summary per course.

IMPORTANT:
- Multiple instructors appear in one row.
- Repeated identical names or usernames are removed.
- Names and usernames are aggregated separately.
- Positions in the two lists are not guaranteed
  to represent corresponding faculty members.
- PERSON deletion, availability, and enabled
  status are not checked.
- Instructor enrollment availability and enabled
  status are not checked.
- Primary instructor status is not evaluated.

------------------------------------------------------------
MAIN QUERY
------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE:
Combines course, term, AI Conversation count,
and instructor information into a course-level report.

COURSE AND TERM JOIN:

INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.TERM t
    ON t.ID = c.TERM_ID

Requires each returned course to have a matching
term record.

AI CONVERSATION JOIN:

INNER JOIN ai_counts a
    ON a.COURSE_SOURCE_ID =
       TRY_TO_NUMBER(c.SOURCE_ID)

Requires each returned course to have matching
AI Conversation assessment records.

TRY_TO_NUMBER:
Attempts to convert COURSE.SOURCE_ID to a number.

If SOURCE_ID cannot be converted to a numeric value,
TRY_TO_NUMBER returns NULL.

Those courses will not match a numeric source identifier
through this join.

IMPORTANT:
Because this is an INNER JOIN, courses with no
matching AI Conversation records are excluded.

Courses with zero AI Conversations do not appear
in the report.

INSTRUCTOR JOIN:

LEFT JOIN instructors i
    ON i.COURSE_ID = c.ID

Adds instructor information when matching
instructor enrollments are available.

Courses without matching instructors remain
in the report, with NULL instructor fields.

------------------------------------------------------------
FIELDS RETURNED
------------------------------------------------------------

1. COURSE_ID
   Blackboard course number from COURSE.COURSE_NUMBER.

2. COURSE_NAME
   Blackboard course name.

3. TERM_NAME
   Academic term name from CDM_LMS.TERM.

4. INSTRUCTOR_NAMES
   Comma-separated list of instructor names.

5. INSTRUCTOR_USERIDS
   Comma-separated list of Blackboard instructor
   usernames extracted from PERSON.STAGE.

6. AI_CONVERSATION_COUNT
   Number of distinct matching AI Conversation
   assessment records associated with the course.

------------------------------------------------------------
COURSE FILTERING CONDITIONS
------------------------------------------------------------

1. c.ROW_DELETED_TIME IS NULL

   Excludes courses marked as deleted.

2. c.COURSE_NUMBER NOT ILIKE 'TEST%'

   Excludes courses whose course number begins
   with TEST, regardless of capitalization.

   Examples excluded:
   - TEST_2026_FA
   - TestCourse101
   - testing_course

   Course numbers that are NULL are also excluded
   because the comparison does not evaluate to TRUE.

3. t.NAME = 'Fall 2026 (All Courses)'

   Restricts results to courses associated with
   the academic term having this exact name.

   IMPORTANT:
   This filter uses the TERM table rather than
   searching for '2026_FA' in the course number.

   The term name must match the specified value.

------------------------------------------------------------
COURSE-LEVEL COUNTING
------------------------------------------------------------

The AI Conversation count is calculated separately
for each course source identifier.

The result is then connected to the corresponding
course record in CDM_LMS.COURSE.

Example:

COURSE_ID                 AI_CONVERSATION_COUNT
PSY_6721_OL_01_2026_FA    5
PSY_6721_OL_02_2026_FA    3
PSY_6721_OL_03_2026_FA    1

Each returned course displays its matching count.

IMPORTANT:
The count does not indicate how many different
faculty members created the assessments.

A course with five AI Conversations and two
instructors will display:
- AI_CONVERSATION_COUNT = 5
- Both instructor names in INSTRUCTOR_NAMES

The count remains associated with the course,
not with each individual instructor.

------------------------------------------------------------
SORTING
------------------------------------------------------------

Results are ordered by:

1. a.AI_COUNT DESC
   Displays courses with the highest AI Conversation
   counts first.

2. c.COURSE_NUMBER
   Sorts courses alphabetically by course number
   when counts are equal.

------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT NOTES
------------------------------------------------------------

- The report focuses on Fall 2026 courses.

- Only courses with matching AI Conversation
  assessment records are returned.

- Courses with zero matching AI Conversations
  are excluded.

- AI_CONVERSATION_COUNT is calculated using
  COUNT(DISTINCT q.PK1).

- Faculty names and usernames are combined
  into comma-separated fields.

- Faculty adoption is inferred from AI Conversation
  assessments existing in courses with instructor
  enrollments, not from verified creator activity.

- The query does not identify who created
  each AI Conversation assessment.

- The query does not measure student participation
  or engagement with AI Conversations.

- The query does not check COURSE.AVAILABLE_IND
  or COURSE.ENABLED_IND.

- The query does not filter deleted or disabled
  PERSON records.

- The query relies on the relationship between
  LEARN.QTI_ASI_DATA.CRSMAIN_PK1 and
  CDM_LMS.COURSE.SOURCE_ID.

- This LEARN relationship and its assessment-type
  fields must be validated against documentation
  outside the supplied CDM schema files.

- No date-range filter is applied to the
  assessment records themselves.

- The query reports counts by matched course
  record, not a unique count by instructor.

*/

-- Fall 2026 AI Conversation Faculty Adoption

WITH ai_counts AS (
    SELECT
        q.CRSMAIN_PK1 AS COURSE_SOURCE_ID,
        COUNT(DISTINCT q.PK1) AS AI_COUNT
    FROM LEARN.QTI_ASI_DATA q
    WHERE q.BBMD_ASSESSMENT_SUBTYPE = 'AiConversation'
      AND q.BBMD_ASI_TYPE = 1
      AND q.ROW_DELETED_TIME IS NULL
    GROUP BY q.CRSMAIN_PK1
),

instructors AS (
    SELECT
        pc.COURSE_ID,

        LISTAGG(
            DISTINCT CONCAT(
                p.FIRST_NAME, ' ', p.LAST_NAME
            ),
            ', '
        ) WITHIN GROUP (
            ORDER BY CONCAT(
                p.FIRST_NAME, ' ', p.LAST_NAME
            )
        ) AS INSTRUCTOR_NAMES,

        LISTAGG(
            DISTINCT p.STAGE:user_id::string,
            ', '
        ) WITHIN GROUP (
            ORDER BY p.STAGE:user_id::string
        ) AS INSTRUCTOR_USERIDS

    FROM CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE pc

    INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.PERSON p
        ON p.ID = pc.PERSON_ID

    WHERE pc.COURSE_ROLE = 'I'
      AND pc.ROW_DELETED_TIME IS NULL

    GROUP BY pc.COURSE_ID
)

SELECT
    c.COURSE_NUMBER AS COURSE_ID,
    c.NAME AS COURSE_NAME,
    t.NAME AS TERM_NAME,
    i.INSTRUCTOR_NAMES,
    i.INSTRUCTOR_USERIDS,
    a.AI_COUNT AS AI_CONVERSATION_COUNT

FROM CDM_LMS.COURSE c

INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.TERM t
    ON t.ID = c.TERM_ID

INNER JOIN ai_counts a
    ON a.COURSE_SOURCE_ID =
        TRY_TO_NUMBER(c.SOURCE_ID)

LEFT JOIN instructors i
    ON i.COURSE_ID = c.ID

WHERE c.ROW_DELETED_TIME IS NULL
  AND c.COURSE_NUMBER NOT ILIKE 'TEST%'
  AND t.NAME = 'Fall 2026 (All Courses)'

ORDER BY
    a.AI_COUNT DESC,
    c.COURSE_NUMBER;
